    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Quillsen is delighted to present No. 5 Raleigh Square to the market.\n\nAn excellent opportunity to acquire a substantial three-bedroom family home with an exceptionally large rear garden, attached garage and enormous potential to extend and transform the existing accommodation, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nRequiring upgrading, No. 5 offers prospective purchasers the opportunity to create a property tailored to their own requirements. \n\nThe ground floor comprises an entrance porch and hall, a living room, separate family room, kitchen and a shower room positioned to the rear. A utility room is attached to the house and is accessed externally from the rear garden.\n\nUpstairs there are three bedrooms, including a spacious main bedroom, together with a family bathroom.\n\nOutside is where No. 5 really comes into its own. The house occupies a remarkably generous site with extensive gardens. The large rear garden offers tremendous scope to extend the existing house while still retaining a substantial garden, subject to planning permission. For buyers looking to undertake a renovation or create a larger family home, the possibilities are considerable.\n\nTo the front is a garden and driveway providing off-street parking, together with an attached garage. \n\nRaleigh Square is a mature residential development in Crumlin, conveniently positioned for the extensive everyday amenities of the surrounding area. Local shops, schools and recreational facilities are all within easy reach. The location also offers convenient access to a number of bus routes and the wider road network.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\n\nEntrance Porch & Hallway\nEntrance porch opening to the main hallway.\n\nLiving Room - 3.98m (13'1\") x 3.38m (11'1\")\nWell-proportioned reception room with timber flooring, fireplace and built-in shelving.\n\nFamily Room - 3.2m (10'6\") x 5.79m (19'0\")\nGenerous second reception room providing flexible additional family living space.\n\nKitchen - 3.35m (11'0\") x 2.32m (7'7\")\nFitted kitchen with a range of floor and wall units, timber-effect worktops, tiled splashbacks and window providing natural light.\n\nShower Room - 1.67m (5'6\") x 2.72m (8'11\")\nGround floor shower room with shower enclosure, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nUtility Room\nUseful additional utility room attached to the house and accessed externally from the rear garden.\n\nFirst Foor\n\nLanding\n\nPrincipal Bedroom - 4.96m (16'3\") x 2.99m (9'10\")\nA spacious principal bedroom to the front.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.2m (10'6\") x 3.88m (12'9\")\nDouble room to the front.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.99m (9'10\") x 2.47m (8'1\")\nSingle Room to rear.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 1.98m (6'6\") x 1.83m (6'0\")\nFamily bathroom serving the first-floor accommodation.\n\nOutside\nFront Garden / Driveway\nGenerous front garden with driveway providing valuable off-street parking and access to the attached garage.\n\nGarage\nAttached garage providing excellent storage and offering potential for conversion or incorporation into the main house, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nRear Garden\nAn outstanding feature of the property is the exceptionally large rear garden. The sheer depth and scale of the garden provide obvious scope for a substantial extension to the existing house, subject to planning permission, while still allowing for the retention of a generous family garden.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Substantial three-bedroom family home </li><li> Exceptional potential to extend and reconfigure, subject to planning permission </li><li> Large rear garden </li><li> Generous front garden and off-street parking </li><li> Attached garage </li><li> Additional utility room accessed from rear garden </li><li> Excellent opportunity for both buyers seeking a renovation project or investors</li></ul>"
      },
